post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

crowndictator reads /dev/input directly to catch its push-to-talk chord on any
compositor, so it needs read access there. Add yourself to the input group and
log back in:

    sudo usermod -aG input "$USER"

To type transcriptions into the focused window it looks for `wtype`, then
`ydotool` (with ydotoold running); without either it falls back to copying to
the clipboard through `wl-copy`.

The shortcut, microphone and GPU switch come from ~/.config/crownos/input.ron,
which the CrownOS settings panel writes and the daemon follows live.

The Parakeet TDT model downloads from Hugging Face on first use — roughly
700 MB for the int8 (CPU) variant, 2.5 GB for fp32 (CUDA).

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  :
}
